<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 3.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 3.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on January 2. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name			   P/E	 Close</p>
<p>1   Tourism Asset		3666.67    1.10</p>
<p>2   Portman Min		   373.02    2.35</p>
<p>3   Niugini Min		   223.02    3.10</p>
<p>4   Mayne Nickless		186.98    8.47</p>
<p>5   Adel Bton Cement	    123.19    1.70</p>
<p>6   Colonial Coml		 122.95    2.25</p>
<p>7   Forrestania Gold	     87.81    2.45</p>
<p>8   Westral Forest		 85.14    2.35</p>
<p>9   Herald Rsc		     84.96    0.96</p>
<p>10  Countrywide-PP		 83.94    1.15</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p>1   Dominion Min		    2.25    0.98</p>
<p>2   Consol Rutile		   3.15    0.89</p>
<p>3   Computer Power		  3.76    3.85</p>
<p>4   Premier Inv		     4.23    0.75</p>
<p>5   Queensland Cotton	     5.78    4.39</p>
<p>6   Parbury Ltd		     6.25    0.74</p>
<p>7   BTR Plc			   6.45    6.00</p>
<p>8   OLS Asia Hldgs		  7.39    0.88</p>
<p>9   Aust Gold Rsc		   7.51    1.37</p>
<p>10  FAI Life ltd		    7.96    0.82</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
